    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1146-a1">

                <pb facs="1148" n="982" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg982"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Subsecretary of Foreign
                            Affairs to Ambassador Fletcher
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">1922</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: In due reply to the attentive
                    note of your excellency dated October 23, last, I have the honor to transmit a
                        list<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1146-f1"/> containing the names of <pb
                        facs="1149" n="983" xml:id="pg983"/> Americans naturalized as Mexicans from
                    the preconstitutional epoch to the present date.</p>
                <p>Also, replying to the interrogation of your excellency in this connection, I am
                    pleased to state that the foreigners should only renounce their nationality in
                    so far as affecting the property acquired and not in an absolute manner,
                    according to Fraction I of Article 27 of the Political Constitution of the
                    Republic.</p>
                <p>Be pleased [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Garza Perez</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
